 *  @ingroup midifileplayer_management
 *  @brief Extended loading, looping, and transition features available in Maestro Pro.
 */

/** @page midifileplayer_overview MidiFilePlayer Overview
 *  @brief Understand the role of MidiFilePlayer in Maestro MPTK.
 *
 *  @details
 *  MidiFilePlayer is the high-level component used to play complete MIDI files with the
 *  MidiFilePlayer prefab. It is suitable for simple playback driven entirely from the inspector,
 *  but it also exposes a scripting API for interactive and gameplay-oriented scenarios.
 *
 *  Typical use cases include:
 *  - selecting a MIDI by name or index,
 *  - playing or looping a track,
 *  - changing speed,
 *  - seeking by time or by tick,
 *  - receiving callbacks at start, end, or on groups of MIDI events,
 *  - preloading a MIDI to inspect or modify its events before playback.
 *
 *  MidiFilePlayer inherits from MidiSynth, so playback-oriented features are documented here,
 *  while sound generation and channel processing are inherited from MidiSynth.
 *
 *  @section mfp_overview_quick_start Quick Start
 *  - Add the MidiFilePlayer prefab to the scene.
 *  - Choose a MIDI from the MidiDB (name or index).
 *  - Call @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Play "MPTK_Play()".
 *
 *  @section mfp_overview_when_to_use When to Use MidiFilePlayer
 *  Prefer MidiFilePlayer when:
 *  - you play complete songs from MIDI files,
 *  - transport controls (play/pause/seek/loop) are central,
 *  - timeline information is needed for UI or gameplay synchronization.
 *
 *  @see @ref midifileplayer_management
 *  @see @ref midifileplayer_loading
 *  @see @ref midifileplayer_playback
 */

/** @page midifileplayer_loading Loading and Inspecting MIDI Content
 *  @brief Load MIDI files and inspect their event data.
 *
 *  @details
 *  MidiFilePlayer can load MIDI content before playback so that your application can inspect,
 *  filter, or alter the event stream.
 *
 *  @section mfp_loading_workflow Typical Workflow
 *  - select a MIDI with MPTK_MidiName or MPTK_MidiIndex,
 *  - call @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Load "MPTK_Load()",
 *  - inspect @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_MidiLoaded "MPTK_MidiLoaded",
 *  - optionally read events with @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_ReadMidiEvents "MPTK_ReadMidiEvents()",
 *  - then call @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Play "MPTK_Play(alreadyLoaded: true)".
 *
 *  @section mfp_loading_pro Pro Sources
 *  Maestro Pro also adds:
 *  - loading from a desktop file path,
 *  - playing from a byte array,
 *  - playing from a MPTKWriter object.
 *
 *  For script-based MIDI authoring, see @ref mptkwriter_concept.
 *
 *  @section mfp_loading_note Important Note
 *  Always check that @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_MidiLoaded "MPTK_MidiLoaded"
 *  is not null before reading loaded MIDI information.
 *
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Load
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_ReadMidiEvents
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_MidiLoaded
 *  @see @ref mptkwriter_concept
 */

/** @page midifileplayer_playback Playback Control Workflow
 *  @brief Control playback start, stop, pause, restart, and track navigation.
 *
 *  @details
 *  MidiFilePlayer provides a compact API for transport control.
 *
 *  @section mfp_playback_transport Transport Controls
 *  Common operations:
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Play "MPTK_Play()" starts playback,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Stop "MPTK_Stop()" stops playback,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Pause "MPTK_Pause()" pauses playback,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_UnPause "MPTK_UnPause()" resumes playback,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_RePlay "MPTK_RePlay()" restarts the current MIDI,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Next "MPTK_Next()" and @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Previous "MPTK_Previous()" navigate the MidiDB list.
 *
 *  @section mfp_playback_options Playback Options
 *  Additional options allow starting at the first note, stopping on the last note,
 *  auto-restarting, and controlling how playback stops relative to voice release/end.
 *
 *  @section mfp_playback_common_mistakes Common Mistakes
 *  - Calling play before MIDI selection/loading is valid.
 *  - Assuming stop behavior ignores release tails without checking stop options.
 *  - Mixing timeline-based logic with random next/previous navigation without state tracking.
 *
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Play
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Stop
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Pause
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_UnPause
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_RePlay
 */

/** @page midifileplayer_position Position and Timing
 *  @brief Work with playback position, ticks, duration, and speed.
 *
 *  @details
 *  MidiFilePlayer exposes both musical and real-time representations of playback.
 *
 *  @section mfp_position_time_models Time Models
 *  Use:
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Position "MPTK_Position" for time-based seeking in milliseconds,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_TickCurrent "MPTK_TickCurrent" for tick-based seeking,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Duration "MPTK_Duration" and @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_DurationMS "MPTK_DurationMS" for total duration,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_PlayTime "MPTK_PlayTime" and @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_RealTime "MPTK_RealTime" for elapsed playback time,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Pulse "MPTK_Pulse" and @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_DeltaTicksPerQuarterNote "MPTK_DeltaTicksPerQuarterNote" for timing analysis,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Speed "MPTK_Speed" to accelerate or slow down playback.
 *
 *  This separation is useful when your application mixes musical timing,
 *  UI displays, and gameplay synchronization.
 *
 *  @section mfp_position_best_practices Best Practices
 *  - Use ticks for musical-grid logic.
 *  - Use milliseconds for UI clocks and user-facing displays.
 *  - Apply @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Speed "MPTK_Speed" carefully when synchronizing external systems.
 *
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Position
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_TickCurrent
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Duration
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Speed
 */

/** @page midifileplayer_events Playback Events and Unity Callbacks
 *  @brief React to playback start, end, and MIDI event groups.
 *
 *  @details
 *  MidiFilePlayer exposes Unity events that let your application react to playback state changes
 *  and to groups of MIDI events as they are about to be played.
 *
 *  @section mfp_events_callbacks Main Callbacks
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.OnEventStartPlayMidi "OnEventStartPlayMidi": fired when playback is initialized and ready to begin,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.OnEventEndPlayMidi "OnEventEndPlayMidi": fired when playback ends or stops for a specific reason,
 *  - @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.OnEventNotesMidi "OnEventNotesMidi": fired for groups of MIDI events on the same tick.
 *
 *  @section mfp_events_use_cases Typical Use Cases
 *  These hooks are especially useful for gameplay synchronization, visualization,
 *  and runtime interaction with the MIDI stream.
 *
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.OnEventStartPlayMidi
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.OnEventEndPlayMidi
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.OnEventNotesMidi
 */

/** @page midifileplayer_pro MidiFilePlayer Pro Extensions
 *  @brief Extended playback, loading, and looping options available in Maestro Pro.
 *
 *  @details
 *  Maestro Pro extends MidiFilePlayer with advanced workflows such as:
 *  - inner-loop control,
 *  - dedicated inner-loop workflow guide: @ref mptkinnerloop_concept,
 *  - loading MIDI files from local desktop paths,
 *  - playing from byte arrays,
 *  - playing from MPTKWriter-generated data,
 *  - delayed transitions, fade-in, fade-out, and indexed navigation helpers.
 *
 *  @section mfp_pro_external External MIDI Sources
 *  - Local file playback (desktop path): use @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Load "MPTK_Load(string uri)" and then @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Play "MPTK_Play(alreadyLoaded: true)".
 *  - Web URL playback (`http://` / `https://`) and `file://` URI playback: use @ref MidiPlayerTK.MidiExternalPlayer "MidiExternalPlayer" (Pro), which is dedicated to external MIDI URIs.
 *
 *  @section mfp_pro_usage Typical Pro Usage
 *  These additions are useful for:
 *  - dynamic in-game music transitions,
 *  - external user-provided MIDI content (local files and web-hosted MIDI),
 *  - generated MIDI playback pipelines.
 *
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_InnerLoop
 *  @see @ref mptkinnerloop_concept
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Load
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiExternalPlayer
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_Play
 *  @see MidiPlayerTK.MidiFilePlayer.MPTK_SwitchMidiWithDelay
 *  @see @ref maestro_pro_features
 *  @see @ref mptkwriter_concept
 */
